opencode returned COMMENT and Claude APPROVE, so the stricter one is binding.
Every point from both is acted on.

**The grid had no in-app entry point.** The route existed and nothing linked to
it: a user in t3code could not find the watch view, and the tests reached it by
typing a URL. The sidebar has a "Builders" link now, gated on
`hasCodevHierarchy` so a workspace with no Codev agents sees nothing new — the
same rule the tree follows.

**The width was measured two ways.** Mount read `getBoundingClientRect().width`,
the BORDER box; `ResizeObserver` reported `contentRect.width`, which already has
padding removed; `contentWidth` then subtracted the padding again from one of
them. Near a column boundary the layout would flip after the first observe. The
padding moved to an inner wrapper, so the observed box has none and both paths
report the same number.

**Orphans were dropped.** A builder whose architect was archived is still a
running agent — the phase 7 reasoning exactly — and a watch view that omitted it
would hide the agent a human is most likely to be looking for. They tile.

**Two things the DOM was saying that were not true.**
`data-codev-architect-placement` read `"strip"` on a page with no architect at
all; it reads `"none"` there now. And the header said "N builders" while N+2
tiles rendered in the multi-architect case.

`--codev-pane-body` was set on the grid and consumed nowhere, with the panes
carrying a literal `text-[13px]` — a second copy of a number `layout.ts` owns.
The pane inherits the property now.

The route ran `buildCodevSidebarOrder` twice on the same input; once.

**And the sidebar is 256px, not the 232 the comments claimed.** Every conclusion
survives — 1440 open is 1184 of grid and still three columns, 1920 open is 1664
and still four — but the unit tests were written against invented numbers. They
use the real ones, and 1440 with the sidebar COLLAPSED turns out to fit four
columns, so the architect gets a tile there. That is the rule working, not an
exception to it: the user made room for a fourth column and 4 + 3 is not ragged.

